<title>THAILAND: Thai cabinet approves 59 billion baht budget cut.</title>
<headline>Thai cabinet approves 59 billion baht budget cut.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai cabinet on Tuesday approved a finance ministry proposal to cut the 1997/1998 (October-September) fiscal budget by 59 billion baht ($1.9 billion) in line with an austerity package sponsored by the International Monetary Fund (IMF).</p>
<p>Virat Wattanasiritham, secretary general of the National Economic and Social Development Board (NESDB), said the cut would trim next year's government spending to 923 billion baht compared with 925 billion for the current year.</p>
</text>
